Package: xquest
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 xquest-data (>= 1.3),
Description: XQuest arcade shooter — SDL2 port for Linux
 XQuest is a fast-paced top-down arcade shooter originally written for
 DOS by Mark Mackey in 1994.  This package is a faithful SDL2 port for
 modern Linux desktops.
 .
 Pilot a spaceship through 50 levels, collecting crystals to open the
 exit gate while avoiding or destroying 18 distinct enemy types.
 Features powerups, smart bombs, a 3-D starfield, PCM sound effects,
 and a persistent high-score table.

Package: xquest-data
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: xquest
Description: XQuest arcade shooter — original game data files
 This package contains the original XQuest v1.3 game data: sprites,
 enemy definitions, font, sound effects, and the title-screen bitmap.
 .
 These files were created by Mark Mackey and are released as freeware.
 See /usr/share/doc/xquest-data/copyright for the full licence terms.
